<title>USA: Albright plans nine stops on Europe, Asia tour.</title>
<headline>Albright plans nine stops on Europe, Asia tour.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Secretary of State Madeleine Albright is expected to visit nine European and Asian capitals on her first overseas trip next month, U.S. officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>Although they insist plans are not final, officials said the intinerary includes London, Paris, Bonn, Brussels, Rome, Moscow, Tokyo, Seoul and Beijing. The trip would be from Feb. 15 to Feb. 25.</p>
<p>Albright will make a final decision about the trip over the weekend and then her travel plans will be formally announced next week, officials said.</p>
<p>U.S. secretaries of state usually make their first trip to Europe. But Albright, an expert on Europe, is making a swing that also includes Asia to emphasise the importance the United States assigns to that region and to acquaint herself with an area she is not as familiar with.</p>
</text>
